# @epistemologic/property/cold_compile_within_tolerance — the
# DECLARATIVE HALF of the second ouroboros bite. Substrate-pull-correct
# property asserting: cold compile time across substrate-pull ticks
# is bounded by baseline × (1 + tolerance).
#
# Tick 43 / second ouroboros bite. Per Taut's substrate-decl analysis
# 2026-06-19: this IS the lift that WOULD have caught yesterday's
# 38-min pre-push hang. The first ouroboros bite (dark_count_monotone
# at tick 41) was safe but didn't catch real regressions; this bite
# catches the regression class today's hang exposed.
#
# === The bilateral pattern (#53; fourth instance) ===
#
# - First: @kintsugi/fracture/keyword (2026-06-10 `d908798`)
# - Second: @mirror/fracture/predicate (forward-promised, #272)
# - Third: dark_count_monotone (yesterday tick 41, `499ffd9`)
# - Fourth (THIS): cold_compile_within_tolerance
#
# Declarative half: this property
# Operational half: @kintsugi/fracture/cold_compile_within_tolerance
#                    (sibling shard in this same tick)
#
# === The predicate ===
#
# Per @mirror/bench's three-conjunct monotone_non_increasing
# (substrate-mathematical floor for eⁿ⁺¹ ≤ eⁿ at op-runtime altitude),
# specialized to the cold_compile operation:
#
#   cold_compile_within_tolerance(crate, baseline, current,
#                                 tolerance) ⇔
#     runtime_ns(current) ≤ runtime_ns(baseline) × (1 + tolerance)
#   ∧ output_oid(current)  ≡ output_oid(baseline)
#   ∧ env_oid(current)     ≡ env_oid(baseline)
#
# Three-conjunct guards against false-positives:
# - perf conjunct: the substrate-mathematical regression check
# - output conjunct: same binary produced (correctness)
# - env conjunct: same hardware+toolchain+flags (no cross-machine
#                 false-positive)
#
# === Why this lift catches yesterday's regression ===
#
# Yesterday's 38-min cold compile (vs ~25s warm) was a substrate
# regression: same op, same env, same expected output, BUT runtime
# exploded. The three-conjunct's perf check fails with verdict
# `failure`; the fracture body (sibling shard) emits a re-bench
# morphism that the kintsugi loop applies, refusing the push gate
# until cold compile returns within tolerance.
#
# This IS the substrate disclosure Alex's framing #2 named: regression
# tests fail when the same operation becomes slower (with an error
# delta).
#
# === Crystal storage shape (per @mirror/bench bench_crystal) ===
#
# Both baseline and current are bench_crystals at perf altitude. The
# fracture_calendar from Mara's @mirror/store/crystal (the existing
# build-lifecycle altitude crystal) names WHEN to re-bench. The
# predecessor-OID chain at perf altitude tracks the cold_compile
# crystal evolution.
#
# === Composes with @mirror/bench ===
#
# This property's verdict feeds @mirror/bench's regress_check via
# composition. When the kintsugi loop runs cold_compile_within_
# tolerance against the current bench_crystal, the verdict gates
# whether the substrate-pull tick is admissible. The pre-push gate
# becomes substrate-pull-correct: regress → imperfect → hold the
# push until re-converge.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   compile-time budgets       webpack/parcel/turborepo bundle-size
#                              budgets at the build-tool altitude.
#                              This property lifts to substrate-decl.
#   Criterion.rs threshold     Bencher discipline of failing CI when
#                              perf regresses past threshold.
#                              Substrate-altitude equivalent.
#   monotone ranking functions Floyd-Hoare loop invariants;
#                              cold_compile_ns IS a ranking function
#                              for substrate-pull-tick admissibility.
#
# Spec context: shards/mirror/bench.mirror (#87; the bench substrate-
#               decl this property composes via monotone_non_
#               increasing); shards/epistemologic/property/
#               dark_count_monotone.mirror (the THIRD bilateral
#               instance; this shard is the FOURTH).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-mirror-bench-ouroboros]] (#87;
#                       this property is the second ouroboros bite),
#                      [[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]
#                       (#53 pattern; this is the fourth instance),
#                      [[architecture-loop-as-monad]] (#88; the
#                       loop's bind action's pact-respected cascades
#                       through this property),
#                      [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (crate and
#                       bench_crystal are typed carriers).
# Related shards: mirror/bench.mirror (the bench substrate-decl;
#                  monotone_non_increasing is the three-conjunct
#                  this property specializes),
#                 epistemologic/property/dark_count_monotone.mirror
#                  (sibling third instance; substrate-pull-pattern
#                  ancestor),
#                 kintsugi/fracture/cold_compile_within_tolerance.mirror
#                  (the OPERATIONAL HALF of this bilateral pair;
#                  landed in this same tick).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/epistemologic/property/cold_compile_within_tolerance.mirror`
# declares `@epistemologic/property/cold_compile_within_tolerance`
# per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/programming/floyd-hoare-1969
source @arxiv/programming/bencher-criterion-2014

# === The crate carrier ===
#
# Typed reference for the Rust crate being benched. Forward-promised
# refinement: typed parametric crate once the substrate's cargo-
# manifold type lands.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type crate = ref

# === cold_compile_within_tolerance predicate (declarative half) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING PREDICATE. Returns verdict that the current cold
# compile crystal's runtime is bounded by baseline × (1 + tolerance)
# under same output_oid and same env_oid.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the @kintsugi loop's
# active_pass reads this predicate during the pre-push gate. The
# operational half (the fracture body that emits a re-bench morphism
# when this predicate fails) lives at
# @kintsugi/fracture/cold_compile_within_tolerance (sibling shard in
# this same tick).
#
# Bounded → substrate-pull is honest (cold compile within tolerance,
# same binary, same env). Unbounded → substrate-pull regressed; the
# kintsugi loop must re-converge before the push is admissible.
cold_compile_within_tolerance(
  c: crate,
  baseline: bench_crystal,
  current: bench_crystal,
  tolerance: metric
) -> verdict { \ }

out @epistemologic/property/cold_compile_within_tolerance
out crate
out cold_compile_within_tolerance
